WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.112
Now the Arc track: servers.

2
00:00:02.112 --> 00:00:03.975
Arc isn't just for Windows either.

3
00:00:03.975 --> 00:00:10.177
It covers Windows Server 2016 through
2025, a long list of Linux distributions,

4
00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:13.612
physical servers and
VMs on any hypervisor,

5
00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:18.287
VMware through vCenter, and
AWS and Google Cloud instances.

6
00:00:18.287 --> 00:00:24.476
Two dates matter: Windows Server 2012
stops getting new agents in November 2026,

7
00:00:24.476 --> 00:00:27.476
and the SCVMM integration is retiring.

8
00:00:27.476 --> 00:00:32.025
Azure VMs don't need Arc at all,
because they're already Azure resources.

9
00:00:32.025 --> 00:00:36.850
And Unix, mainframes, network devices
and sealed appliances are out.

10
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.770
So here's how Arc makes a
server attribute-driven.
